# Findings gitleaks reports that are not secrets, by fingerprint:
#
#   <commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>   the commit that added the line, and the
#                                   line's number in that commit
#
# Only this form. gitleaks also accepts <file>:<rule>:<line>, but it checks
# every finding of a git scan against that form too: such an entry would hide
# any NEW finding later made on the same line of the same file, and it goes
# stale without a word when the file shifts. A fingerprint names one finding in
# one commit; a line that changes is reported again and decided again. A
# directory scan (`gitleaks dir .`) is not what CI runs, and it reports the
# findings below; that is expected.
#
# Each fingerprint below is the one gitleaks 8.24.3 printed for it.

